 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 01:58:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 040/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-surya: fix WCD9375 TX
 port mapping

The TX port map was off by one: it mapped the codec's ADC1 device port
onto SoundWire port 1, ADC2/3 onto port 1, and the DMIC groups onto
ports 2 and 3.

SoundWire port 1 on this link is PCM_OUT1 and carries no capture data,
so the TX macro read a port the codec never streamed on. Everything
looked healthy - the codec probed, the whole DAPM capture chain powered
up (MIC BIAS1, AMIC1, ADC1, TX SWR_ADC0, TX DEC0 MUX and TX_AIF1 CAP all
On), the PCM opened and the DMA ran - but capture returned digital
silence: exactly 0 after the ADC's DC settling transient, with no noise
floor at all, which is not something a live analogue ADC can produce.

The binding documents the correct mapping for this codec:

  WCD9370 TX Port 1 (ADC1)               <=> SWR2 Port 2
  WCD9370 TX Port 2 (ADC2, 3)            <=> SWR2 Port 2
  WCD9370 TX Port 3 (DMIC0,1,2,3 & MBHC) <=> SWR2 Port 3
  WCD9370 TX Port 4 (DMIC4,5,6,7)        <=> SWR2 Port 4

which is <2 2 3 4>, and matches the downstream sm6150/sdmmagpie port map
for this board (sdmmagpie is SM7150 downstream): <2 ADC1 0x1>,
<2 ADC2 0x2>, <3 ADC3 0x1>, <4 DMIC0..3>, <5 DMIC4..7>, with port 1
reserved for PCM_OUT1.

With this the microphone captures: a sustained noise floor across the
whole recording (~92% non-zero samples instead of zeros), and the ADC1
gain control scales it monotonically (RMS 3.1 -> 6.0 -> 41.3 for gain
0 -> 10 -> 20), confirming the analogue path is live.

Signed-off-by: Edi <woodyst@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
index 6410fe3b5..61522e859 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ &swr2 {			/* TX */
 	wcd9375_tx: codec@0,3 {
 		compatible = "sdw20217010a00";
 		reg = <0 3>;
-		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <1 1 2 3>;
+		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <2 2 3 4>;
 		qcom,tx-channel-mapping = /bits/ 8 <1 2 1 1 2 3 3 4 1 2 3 4>;
 	};
 };
